WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.560
SCP-066 was once a wholesome, music-loving ball of&nbsp;
colorful living yarn known colloquially as Eric’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.280
Toy. However, while this came to the Foundation&nbsp;
as a relatively benign and friendly creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.960
the actions of the Foundation itself&nbsp;
soon turned this anomaly sour.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.920
During a test, a Foundation Researcher cut&nbsp;
a thread from SCP-066, causing it not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.480
considerable pain and distress but also making&nbsp;
it lose all trust in the Foundation. It went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.200
from being a happy ball of ribbon that would&nbsp;
change into friendly forms like cats and produce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.280
birthday cupcakes for researchers, to an angry&nbsp;
little twisted knot of wretched flesh-like twine.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.320
It seems that SCP-066 holds a grudge for&nbsp;
the way it was treated too. Now it regularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.440
deafens researchers and guards in its proximity&nbsp;
with loud music in revenge for its mutilation.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.520
Oh and why do they call it Eric’s Toy?&nbsp;
When it’s not producing ear shattering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.520
music to mess with the researchers and other&nbsp;
anomalous effects, it can be heard saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.800
the name “Eric” in a deep, masculine voice,&nbsp;
though who this Eric is, we just don’t know.

